  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  product-mixer target differs from the true corner on 7/16 blocks

  'deg1'/'deg2' are the squared Walsh weights at each degree. 'ham' is the
  Hamming distance from the surrogate corner to the true one; 'regret' is
  the energy left on the table as a fraction of the hypercube's range.

  A product mixer cannot represent a target that is not the sign pattern of
  the degree-1 coefficients, so ham1 > 0 is a REACHABILITY failure, not a
  signal-to-noise one - and therefore outside what Cerezo & Coles forbids.
  regret2 << regret1 would price the 2-body mixer exactly.
